ERA: WWII (TO&E 10-147, 26 May 1943)
THEATER: PTO (US equipment)  -- ETO used British mobile bakery sets
→ 621.8 / 664 → Mechanical Equipment / Food Tech

FUNDAMENTALS
  breadShare          : ~10% of total food consumed
  servingsPerDay      : 3
  moraleWeight        : highest single ration item
  dailyIssueTarget    : 8 oz per man
  companyCapacity     : 40,000 men  (4 platoons)
  companyOutput       : ~32,000 lb bread / day (US type)

VARIABLES / ORGANIZATION (one platoon)
  platoonCommander    : 2LT / 1LT     weapon = M1 Carbine
  platoonSergeant     : SSgt          weapon = M1 Carbine

  sections            : 4
  perSection:
    sectionLeader     : Sgt           weapon = M1 Carbine or M1903A3/A1 + M1 GL
    baker             : T4            same
    baker             : T5            same
    baker             : Pfc/Pvt       same
    bakerHelper       : Pfc/Pvt x2    same
    generalMechanic   : T5            same
    basic             : Pvt           same

EQUIPMENT (per section)
  ovens               : 2 x M1942 Army Field Bake Oven
  mixer               : 1 x gasoline-engine dough mixer

NOTES
  - Bakers were armed; grenade launchers issued 1 per 4 EM below SSgt/T3
  - PTO units frequently ran 24-hour shifts due to humidity, water, and double load
  - ETO companies were smaller, more mobile, and higher-output with British gear
